D	const_serial_cursor.dawn	349	355	`Cursor` is not a constant-serializable type	a cursor is a position in the backend's own representation of a string, and the two backends do not agree on it, so there is no one value to fold; hold the string and walk to the position where it is used (spec §7.2)
D	const_serial_cursor.dawn	385	397	`List[Cursor]` is not a constant-serializable type	constants hold Int/Float/Bool/String/Unit and List/tuple/record/ADT values built from them (spec §7.2)
